    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Architectural Interest",
            "paragraphs": [
                "The Catford House is a public house and community kitchen revitalised through a series of careful interventions by Hayatsu Architects, commissioned by Lewisham Council as part of a wider town centre regeneration scheme led by Turner Works. Formerly open until 2019 as the Catford Constitutional Club, the building has at its core a locally-listed Georgian farmhouse dating from 1736, Catford’s oldest extant building. The project involved sensitive restoration, introducing new timber structure to stabilise and make accessible the cordoned-off Georgian section, threading new services through the historic fabric, and creating new public realm connections to future mixed-use developments."
            ]
        }
